    "intro_html":  "Ropa vieja means old clothes, which is what shredded beef in a pepper and tomato sauce apparently looked like to whoever named it. It is Cuba\u0027s national dish, it is built for a long slow cook, and the olives at the end are not optional. They are the salt and the sharpness that make the whole pot work. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
